@startuml sequence-wf3
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
autonumber
title Workflow 3: several reports -> duplicates and related incidents found -> correlated and escalated

actor "Employee A" as A
actor "Employee B" as B
actor "Employee C" as C
participant "IncidentService\n<<Facade>>" as SVC
participant "DuplicateDetector\n(TF-IDF or Gemini embeddings\n+ hybrid score)" as DUP
participant "DependencyGraph\n(BFS over depends_on)" as GRAPH
participant "SLAMonitor" as MON
participant "EscalationHandler chain\n<<Chain of Responsibility>>" as CHAIN
participant "NotificationService" as NOTIF
actor Technician
actor "Team Lead" as LEAD
actor Administrator as ADMIN

== The shared service fails first ==
A -> SVC : report "Database cluster down" (P1, Gold: respond in 5 min)
SVC --> A : INC-1 ASSIGNED to a database technician

== Three payment reports ==
B -> SVC : report "Fee portal payment fails" (INC101)
SVC -> DUP : check(): no open look-alike
SVC --> B : INC101 assigned
C -> SVC : POST /incidents/similar while typing
SVC -> DUP : check(title, description, service)
DUP --> C : INC101, score 0.8 >= threshold (shown, never forced)
C -> SVC : report anyway (INC102)
SVC --> C : INC102 assigned; DUPLICATE_SUGGESTED audited
A -> SVC : report with follow = INC101 (INC103)
SVC -> SVC : record INC103, cancel it at once as DUPLICATE of INC101 (D-031)
SVC --> A : "You are now following INC101"

== Technician confirms a duplicate ==
Technician -> SVC : POST /incidents/INC102/confirm-duplicate {INC101}
SVC -> SVC : INC102 -> CANCELLED (duplicate), parent_id = INC101 (D-005)
SVC -> NOTIF : (after commit)
NOTIF -> C : "Your report was linked to INC101"

== Correlation ==
ADMIN -> SVC : GET /incidents/INC101/correlation
SVC -> GRAPH : reach(Fee Payment Portal)
GRAPH --> SVC : Fee Payment Portal depends on Database Cluster
SVC --> ADMIN : 2 reports linked; "likely related to INC-1 (open P1 on\nDatabase Cluster): possible root cause"

== Escalation when nobody acknowledges the P1 ==
loop every 30 s of clock time (3 real s at x10)
  MON -> MON : tick(): response target missed?
  MON -> CHAIN : decide_escalation(missed targets)
  CHAIN --> MON : level 1 Team Lead (just after 5 min),\nlevel 2 Administrator (10 min),\nlevel 3 IT Manager (15 min) (BR-08)
  MON -> SVC : incident.escalate(owner, level) -> ASSIGNED
  MON -> NOTIF : "SLA violated" (assignee, Team Lead, admins)\nand "Escalated" (the new owner)
  NOTIF -> LEAD : in-app, email, Telegram
end
note over SVC, NOTIF
  Every step above is a hash-chained audit record (BR-10);
  the admin's integrity check recomputes the chain.
end note
@enduml
